---
import InnerLayout from '../layouts/InnerLayout.astro';
import InnerBlock from '../components/inner/InnerBlock.astro';
import { SITE_URL, type PageSeo } from '../lib/seo';

const seo: PageSeo = {
  title: 'Careers | Paradius LLC',
  description:
    'We do not hire headcount. We find the ones with the spark and push them further than they believed they could go.',
  canonical: `${SITE_URL}/careers/`,
  webPageName: 'Careers at Paradius',
  webPageDescription:
    'How engineers join Paradius: referrals, the hub, the mentor, and the push.',
};
---

<InnerLayout seo={seo} mode="two-sided">
  <InnerBlock force="will" kind="hero" title="Careers">
    <p>
      We do not hire headcount. We find the ones with the spark and push them further
      than they believed they could go.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="will">
    <p>
      What that means in practice: you start at our hub in Managua, a senior mentor at
      the next desk, standards enforced from day one. Then you go remote, and nothing
      degrades, because the discipline travels with you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Performance pays. Bonuses are tied to what you ship, and training is continuous:
      multicultural communication, languages, the platforms you have not touched yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      On client systems you will carry a code instead of a name. The glory goes to the
      client. The growth stays with you.
    </p>
    <p>For engineers: a place where your spark is an asset, not a liability.</p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" kind="cta">
    <p>
      Designed by an engineer, for engineers. Nobody here is disposable. Almost nobody
      leaves.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are no open positions listed. We find people through referrals and by
      watching who builds what. If you think we should be watching you, write:
      <a href="mailto:solutions@paradius.dev">solutions@paradius.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>
</InnerLayout>
